{"title":"Split Array Minimising Sum of Maxima","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"You are given an array `arr` of `N` positive integers (for example the costs of tasks in a fixed order) and an integer `K`.\n\nSplit the array, **keeping the original order**, into exactly `K` contiguous, **non-empty** pieces. The **cost of a piece** is the maximum element inside it, and the **total cost** of a split is the sum of the costs of its `K` pieces.\n\nPrint the **minimum total cost** over all valid splits.","inputFormat":"The first line contains two integers `N` and `K`.\nThe second line contains `N` space-separated integers `arr[0] ... arr[N-1]`.","outputFormat":"Print a single integer: the minimum total cost.","constraints":["1 ≤ K ≤ N ≤ 300","1 ≤ arr[i] ≤ 10^5"],"examples":[{"input":"5 3\n150 200 400 350 250","output":"750","explanation":"Split into [150], [200], [400, 350, 250]. The costs are 150, 200 and 400, summing to 750. No other split into 3 pieces does better."},{"input":"5 2\n1 5 3 4 2","output":"6","explanation":"[1] and [5, 3, 4, 2] cost 1 + 5 = 6. Every split puts the 5 into some piece, so the total is at least 5 plus the other piece's maximum, which is at least 1."},{"input":"4 4\n9 2 7 3","output":"21","explanation":"With K equal to N each element is its own piece, so the total is the sum of the array."}],"tests":[{"input":"1 1\n5","output":"5"},{"input":"3 1\n3 9 2","output":"9"},{"input":"3 3\n4 4 4","output":"12"},{"input":"2 2\n100000 1","output":"100001"},{"input":"2 2\n1 100000","output":"100001"},{"input":"5 3\n5 4 3 2 1","output":"8"},{"input":"5 3\n1 2 3 4 5","output":"8"},{"input":"2 2\n84 7","output":"91"},{"input":"2 2\n4 2","output":"6"},{"input":"2 1\n17 1","output":"17"},{"input":"3 1\n3 29 86","output":"86"},{"input":"3 3\n2 1 1","output":"4"},{"input":"3 3\n35 14 7","output":"56"},{"input":"4 4\n94 3 1 75","output":"173"},{"input":"4 1\n27 7 11 3","output":"27"},{"input":"4 2\n1 4 1 7","output":"8"},{"input":"5 1\n93 18 65 20 2","output":"93"